    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that sounds like you're just hand-waving the legal reality. the Bruen decision specifically rejected the \"interest-balancing\" test that people used to use to justify all those regulations. if the court says you have to look at history and tradition instead of just \"public safety concerns,\" aren't you basically saying that the current legal standard is wrong? what's the actual legal basis for a regulation to survive if it doesn't have a strong historical precedent?",
